  "caveats": {
    "ghost": "Unreliable. Lakh clean MIDI are largely quantised step-sequenced transcriptions, so ghost-note velocities are flattened; every label measures ~0.00 including Jazz. Use literature targets instead.",
    "swing": "Unreliable for the same reason - real Jazz measures 0.03 here. Use Friberg & Sundstrom (2002) tempo-dependent swing ratios instead.",
    "timingDevMs": "Usable but read with care: the ordering is musically correct (Electronic most quantised at 3.07ms, Blues most human at 19.2ms), but the literature does not support targeting real-human magnitude - Senn et al. (2016) found peak groove ratings near 40% of it.",
    "voiceScoping": "Bass and drum medians are taken only over references that contain that voice, not over all 8 - a reference with no bass cannot measure bass, and counting its silence as a measured zero pulled every bass target low. 9 of 48 references have no bass (funk-rb-06, funk-rb-07, blues-04, blues-06, jazz-05, pop-07, pop-08, electronic-02, electronic-07) and 3 have no drums (blues-04, blues-06, rock-03). Rock is the only genre with no bassless reference, so its bass figures are unchanged from a straight 8-file median. Per-metric sample sizes are recorded as `_metricN` alongside each label; see tools/judge/groove-stats.mjs `aggregate()`."
  },
